# Mutation cases for the `generated-at` pin scan — every committed generated
# tree is watched, not only the ones someone remembered to list.
#
# Run with
# `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/generated_at_scan_reach.cases`.
#
# The roots this test iterates were incomplete until 2026-08-13: Go and Kotlin
# had their W3C `generated` trees listed and their `integration` trees not.
# The omission was not theoretical. Adding one integration stem with the
# per-stem regen scripts — which do not export `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`, only
# `regen_all_committed_trees.sh` does — left a wall-clock stamp in the Rust,
# Go and Kotlin outputs, and this test reported exactly one of the three.
#
# Widening was green on the spot, because all 64 existing integration files
# were already pinned. So the thing the gap cost was never a dirty tree; it was
# the guarantee. That is precisely the shape a coverage claim hides behind, and
# the reason each root needs a case rather than a count.
#
# A case that SURVIVES here means that backend's integration tree is unwatched.

mutation_tests -p sce-build --features cli --test b9_drift_detection

# Read at run time, not compiled in: the test walks these files from disk, so
# the `sce-build` test binary cannot change when one of them does. Declared as
# compiled targets every case below would be INCONCLUSIVE by construction.
mutation_runtime_targets backends/go/tests/integration/parallel_done_state_is_delivered/parallel_done_state_is_delivered_sm.go
mutation_runtime_targets backends/kotlin/tests/src/main/kotlin/com/sce/integration/parallel_done_state_is_delivered/parallel_done_state_is_deliveredSm.kt

# ── Go's integration tree ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The exact value this file carried before it was regenerated with the epoch
# exported. An unpinned regeneration rewrites every file with a fresh
# wall-clock stamp, so the diff reads as churn and hides any real change in it.

mutation_case "an unpinned stamp in the go integration tree" <<'PY'
edit("backends/go/tests/integration/parallel_done_state_is_delivered/parallel_done_state_is_delivered_sm.go",
     "generated-at: 0",
     "generated-at: 1786624467")
PY

# ── Kotlin's integration tree ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# Same stamp, same round, different backend — and the reason both get a case
# rather than one standing for the other: they were two separate missing
# entries in the root list, and a single case would leave whichever root it did
# not touch exactly as unproven as it was before.

mutation_case "an unpinned stamp in the kotlin integration tree" <<'PY'
edit("backends/kotlin/tests/src/main/kotlin/com/sce/integration/parallel_done_state_is_delivered/parallel_done_state_is_deliveredSm.kt",
     "generated-at: 0",
     "generated-at: 1786624467")
PY
